      "notes": "Read-only comparison route over source_digest values reads already return. Takes a bounded array of {id, observed_source_digest} entries for canonical WK-#### work records and resolves each to exactly one of four states: unchanged, changed (carrying current_source_digest so a later check can be re-keyed without a second read), absent (the load reports missing_json_record), or unreadable (present but yielding no usable digest, carrying the loader's diagnostic codes). absent and unreadable stay distinct and neither collapses into changed. It adds no provenance mechanism, no second digest computation, and no tracking: every digest and absence fact comes from the canonical work-record loader. The response uses the repository's bounded-response vocabulary (total_count, returned_count, has_more) and adds unchecked_ids naming every submitted identity that was not resolved, so a truncated answer never reads as a complete one. Digests are the raw sha256:<hex> value, never a compact_read_token, whose embedded issue/expiry times cannot separate an expired token from a changed record.",
      "use_when": [
        "session holds source_digest values from earlier reads and needs to know whether those reads are still current",
        "long-running session must detect a mid-session canonical work-record change before acting on stale context"
      ],
      "do_not_use_when": [
        "record content is needed",
        "a record is being re-read",
        "write precondition enforcement (use the CAS expected_source_digest precondition instead)",
        "no source_digest from a prior read is held"
      ]
