      "notes": "Compact read-only work-record summary for a selected WK or slice. Record-level default output is compact-first: it carries dependencies, review_state, blockers, terminal_review_designation and omission counts, but NOT write_scope, acceptance or validation. Three bounded routes reach what it withholds: unit=<WK-ID>#<slice-id> for one slice, selected_record:true for write_scope, acceptance and validation, and slice_offset/slice_limit/slice_status to page through withheld slices, each page carrying the digest to pass back so a record edited mid-enumeration is reported rather than stitched. None is an expensive option or needs a token first; expensive full or debug reads of large trackers stay refused unless narrowed or acknowledged. Findings rows carry review_purpose: reviewer omission defaults to standalone, explicit redteam standalone is projected, omitted redteam stays absent; non-findings omit it. Record-level output also carries terminal_review_designation: a state of missing, designated, ambiguous or not_applicable plus the exact eligible_count, adding unit_id only when exactly one unit is eligible. Both are advisory and non-authorizing.",
